-- title:
--   Canonical contraction data on translated atlas cells
-- statement:
--   Fix a normalized family of contractions on zero-based intervals of widths at most $S$, with carrier base $m$, common height $K$, and joint bound $J$. A rectangular cell $R$ with positive distinguished width $w_i=R_i^+-R_i^-$ and $w_i\le S$ receives the corresponding width-$w_i$ contraction transported to $[R_i^-,R_i^+]$. Its basepoint is the cell's left bottom point.
--
--   For a tiling whose distinguished widths are bounded by $S$, this defines a contraction provider on every eligible cell. The common track bound is the uniform carrier speed for $m,K$; every cell uses the same previously selected normalized family.
-- source:
--   Ruijun Wang, Continuous graph homomorphisms of higher dimensional abelian group actions, arXiv:2609.39824v1 (2026), Section(s) 4–6; https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.39824v1. This item is auxiliary infrastructure of the accompanying formalization; its implementation definitions are not asserted to be separately numbered in the paper. Original Lean module AbelianTargets/AtlasCanonicalContractions.lean, selected declaration lines 23-28, 46-52; SHA-256 5fa6bd3cd4a1ab5581cdc6d31c30ba0fd6a591fdd2b6fe8cf8598000ee183dc1. Selected spans are from the final generated manifest. The original source snapshot is local; no public repository URL or commit was available.

